Description: Keep the database interface alive as long as a cursor on it is open.
 A cursor holds its statement, but the statement only borrows its SQLite interface, so closing the connection can free
 the interface before the cursor is finalized, and closing the cursor then references freed memory.
 The D-Bus endpoint of the tinysparql command crashed this way with SIGSEGV when it received SIGTERM right after
 serving an export: it closed its connection while a worker thread still finalized the serializer and cursor of the
 last query, which failed a build of the package in the functional test test_cli. The cursor now holds a reference to
 the interface from its creation until it is closed. This is the first commit of the upstream merge request, with its
 regression test, which runs during the build.
 .
 test_cli, run 2000 times with 48 at a time, crashed in test_export_dbus in 10 runs without the patch, always with
 tracker_db_cursor_close() in tracker_db_cursor_finalize() on a worker thread, and in none with it.
